<article class="env-definition" id="0FF3">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FF3">Definition <span data-tag="0FF3">42.59.4</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a local complete intersection morphism of schemes locally of finite type over $S$. We say <em>the Gysin map for $f$ exists</em> if we can write $f = g \circ i$ with $g$ smooth and $i$ an immersion. In this case we define the <em>Gysin map</em> $f^! = i^! \circ g^* \in A^*(X \to Y)$ as above. </p>
</article>